{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they shall be eight boards.</b> Two boards were absorbed in the rear chambers, one to the north and one to the south; six boards remained in the middle in the western wall. And thus it says, ולירכתי המשכן ימה תעשה ששה קרשים, and this verse explains the secret of the indwelling Presence (שכינה), which is in the west, being comprised of six directions. And to allude to this, the west is called by the name ים, for the sea is a receptacle for waters. And the arrangement of the four directions of the world in the supernal Chariot — they are the fathers of the world and David: south first, since Abraham is the first of the fathers, and it is written of him (Genesis 20:1): ״ויסע משם אברהם ארצה הנגב״; north, since Isaac prevailed at the Akedah; east, since it is written of Jacob (Genesis 32:31): ״ויזרח לו השמש״, and they likened Joseph his son to the sun, and the masters of mystery (רז״ל) expounded: Jacob said, who told this one that my name is Shemesh?; west — it is the end, and it is David's lyre that plays of itself, and it is that which is called ים, and this is הים האחרון, whose Aramaic translation is ימה מערבאה. And in order to allude to these four, the four directions of the world were called by these names, and this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:44.957957264Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}